#
# The proprietary NVIDIA driver, from NVIDIA's own repository. Selected by
# DW_NVIDIA=1 install.d/250-nvidia.
#
# Three lines, because that is all the machine this was derived from had installed by
# hand: apt-mark showmanual named nvidia-open, firmware-nvidia-graphics and
# linux-headers-amd64, and the other fifty nvidia packages on it arrived as
# dependencies. Listing those fifty would pin versions this module does not choose.

nvidia-open                     # Driver meta; pulls the open kernel modules, DKMS, the GSP firmware and the libraries
linux-headers-amd64             # What DKMS builds the kernel module against
firmware-nvidia-graphics        # Display firmware, from non-free-firmware rather than from NVIDIA
